    {
      "type": "examAlert",
      "items": [
        "The Shah Commission (1966) was established to demarcate the boundaries for the creation of Haryana.",
        "Charkhi Dadri is frequently tested as the 22nd district of Haryana.",
        "Haryana surrounds the National Capital Territory (NCT) of Delhi on three sides: North, West, and South.",
        "Haryana Day is celebrated annually on 1st November."
      ],
      "id": "v2v7txm"
    },
    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "Haryana was carved out of the former state of East Punjab on 1 November 1966 based on the recommendations of the Shah Commission.",
        "Chandigarh serves as the joint capital of both Haryana and Punjab and hosts the High Court of Punjab and Haryana.",
        "The state is administratively organized into 6 divisions comprising 22 districts, with Charkhi Dadri being the 22nd district created in 2016.",
        "Haryana features a unicameral legislature with 90 seats in the Legislative Assembly (Vidhan Sabha), 10 Lok Sabha seats, and 5 Rajya Sabha seats.",
        "Geographically, Haryana shares borders with 5 states (Punjab, Himachal Pradesh, Uttarakhand, Uttar Pradesh, Rajasthan) and surrounds New Delhi on three sides."
      ],
      "id": "q8zv8ud"
    }
